**How to implement.** S1.1's tabulated case carries optional per-sample one-sigma uncertainties of n and k as data, serialised with the table, so that a material pulled with them keeps them in its entry file, the database payload and a kit's snapshot (001 §D 'PTB OCDB (CC BY 4.0): EUV / VUV n, k with uncertainties', 'Uncertainties travel with the material (PTB's σ) and become priors in studies and inputs to the Planner'; the S13.2 brief 'S1.1's tabulated case gains optional per-sample sigma-n / sigma-k arrays (data, serialised)'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.2. (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`, beside `TabulatedNkTable` (step 2): (a) `TabulatedNkUncertainty`, a record marked `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier("per-sample one-sigma uncertainties of a tabulated n,k table, read beside its columns")>]` with `sigmaN : float array` and `sigmaK : float array`, one value per sample of its table in the table's order. (b) `TabulatedTableError` (step 2) gains `InvalidUncertaintyErr of reason : string`, naming the first offending column and index. (c) `TabulatedNkTable` gains, last, `uncertaintyOpt : TabulatedNkUncertainty option`, with a one-line doc: the source's one-sigma uncertainty of each sample, `None` where the source gives none. `tryCreate` keeps its signature and sets `None`, so every table built today keeps its value. (d) `member this.withUncertainty (sigmaN : float array) (sigmaK : float array) : Result<TabulatedNkTable, TabulatedTableError>` answers the table holding them: two columns whose lengths are not the table's are `SampleCountMismatchErr` naming the lengths, and a NaN, infinite or negative value is `InvalidUncertaintyErr`; it neither sorts nor copies the columns' order. `complexIndex` (step 2) reads no uncertainty, so no number of any table moves. (2) Every complete match on `TabulatedTableError` that FS0025 reports maps the new case as it maps the other three: `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs`' tabulated import (step 2) answers it as `NoDataErr` carrying its reason. The material entry schema is unchanged, because the physics inside a payload is bound by the serializer (step 30), and no committed file changes, because no built-in or committed kit entry is tabulated: the built-in dispersive axes are published laws (step 8; `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:455`, `:476-477`). No interpolation of the uncertainty, option or other member is added: a reader takes a sample's σ from the columns. (3) Tests. `Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs` gains `A tabulated table takes per-sample uncertainties of its own length and refuses any other`: over the hand-written table of step 2's facts (400, 500 and 700 nm), `withUncertainty [| 0.01; 0.02; 0.03 |] [| 0.0; 0.001; 0.002 |]` answers the table holding exactly those columns with `complexIndex` unchanged at each sample (through `BerremanTests.MatrixComparison`'s helpers); columns of two values answer `SampleCountMismatchErr`; a negative, a NaN and an infinite value answer `InvalidUncertaintyErr`; and `tryCreate` answers `uncertaintyOpt = None`. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs` gains `a tabulated material keeps its per-sample uncertainties through an entry file`: a user material whose complexity is one isotropic dispersive segment over that table with those uncertainties round-trips content → `sealed` → `fileText` → `parseEntry` (step 30), its decoded table equal to the original, uncertainties included; and the same material without uncertainties round-trips with `uncertaintyOpt = None`.

**Acceptance.** After the uncertainties land, `TabulatedNkTable` MUST carry `uncertaintyOpt : TabulatedNkUncertainty option`, built only through `withUncertainty`, with every table's numbers unchanged and an entry file keeping the arrays; unit-tests MUST pass over the selected class `BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests`, including `A tabulated table takes per-sample uncertainties of its own length and refuses any other`, the count rising by 1; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a tabulated material keeps its per-sample uncertainties through an entry file`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s44 invariants MUST pass.
